00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.429 align:start position:0%
 
hello and welcome to the new world of  your source for everything anime and  manga and today we are here for some  hunter hunter related fun times quite  specifically to discuss the ever  controversial hypothetical of what would  have happened in the event that adult  gone fought against the ant  king marowan not at all a simple topic  to cover and one that comes with its  fair share of confusion and  misinterpretation which is bound to pop  up in a series like this where the  author you know isn't generally  concerned about power and combat but is  instead  interested in other ideas ideas that are  not power in combat  and actually one of my favorite fun  facts about hunter hunter is that almost  every major fight in the series has been  a completely one-sided affair where the  winner was never realistically in doubt  so we really don't get a lot of truly  equal match-ups and as such it's kind of  a shame that that or gone and meruem  never came face to face because they do  present the pinnacle of raw aura use in  the series but then again  would a well-balanced fight even have  ensued well we're here to explore  exactly that and in order to do so we're  all going to need to take a page from  the book of gone and enhance ourselves  by subscribing to the new world review  which will result in regular hunt onto  content being uploaded straight into  your youtube feed but let's get why into  this topic exists in the first place  i'm sure it was probably still fairly  debated before but the whole adult gone  vs marowan hypothetical really does stem  from the 2011 anime adaptation of hunt  hunter and it's all because of  one line from neferpito where while gone  is transforming they state  i was right his power is now equal to  that of the king  and that is an extraordinarily clear-cut  statement and i really don't blame the  anime-centric part of the fanbase  for simply taking this at face value  especially for a shonen series where  there's always this subconscious  understanding that characters are not  just conveying information for their own  benefit  it's designed not only to speak to  themselves or another character but also  to speak directly to the audience and  when you get into  darker more adult-oriented content this  can change quite a bit by introducing  things to deliberately mislead or  misinform the audience  such as an unreliable narrator and  that's kind of where hunter hunter  actually lands during the chimeran talk  the series very much began its life as a  standard  shonen where every piece of information  could be implicitly trusted however over  time it morphed into something else and  almost every character is now an  unreliable source of information  so when in the anime pito states that  gon's power is now equal to that of the  king that is not  a decree that has been set in stone this  is pito's personal opinion which is  flawed because they don't actually know  the full extent of merome's power nor do  they really grasp the true scope of  adolcons all pitot really knows in this  instant is that both arogon and meruem  are on a level  beyond peter themself and i think that  the manga did a far better job of  portraying pito's feelings on this  matter because in the manga pito's line  was  as i feared his fangs might even sink  into the king which is  completely counter to the anime in the  manga pito is expressing a vague concern  they have no way of quantifying gone as  a threat pito simply senses the  potential of a threat  which to a member of the royal guard is  a matter to be taken with the utmost of  seriousness however there is no talk  whatsoever of being equal to the king  so i just wanted to start by breaking  this myth of equality before we move any  further forward  pito never expresses equality  canonically through the manga and even  if they did  pito's opinion is unreliable however to  have some fun with that you could  potentially even make the argument that  pito is still underestimating gone at  this point and that perhaps he is still  quite close to meruem in terms of power  but we do need to make that assessment  through other means  so firstly let's take a look at meruem  and to be clear we are talking about  meruem prior to absorbing pufa yupi  because what he goes on to become is  essentially a god-like entity and there  is no discussion to be had there  whatsoever  in fact things are kind of tough enough  with just our base for meruem who is the  only character in the entire series who  actually can't be ranked in the hunt  hunter manual because if you take a  brief look at his stats you'll notice  that almost everywhere is a complete  question mark with the exception of one  of the palace invasion set of stats  where everything is five plus which does  very little to clarify anything and  tells us that his capabilities may as  well be infinite on the scale now to put  this into some perspective merome's  primary opponent isaac netro ends his  time in the series with a perfect five  out of five score for each area but even  base four meruem is clearly above that  classification and just while we're  talking about stats i should say that  adolgon does not appear to ever actually  be ranked according to the system  because as far as i can tell all of  these figures refer to regular gone but  for meruem this still tells us quite a  bit in his base form he has  unbeatable well everything speed stamina  strength or  intellect you name it and meruem has  literally all of it  and you have none of it and i do think  it's important to highlight the idea  that marowan was quite deliberately  created as a character who would be  impossible to overcome by traditional  means because  well we tried that we threw humanity's  greatest warrior at meruem and we even  condensed every last drop of his aura  into one gigantic blast and it still was  not enough to do really anything beyond  superficial damage  everything about meruem is intended to  be unbeatable which isn't something we  can really ignore in a hypothetical like  this because for gone to come out on top  here he would essentially need access to  an infinite reserve for power capable of  meeting togashi's intentions behind  meruem but just one more thing regarding  marum there are a lot of minor instances  in the series where people  attempt to bring maorim's abilities down  to some form of reality one of the more  notable ones is right after his birth  where he tail whipped pitot with the  intent to kill them and this event is  something that i often see cited as a  limit to merome's physical power it's a  very poor argument though because having  the intent to kill does not mean using  every ounce of your strength to  accomplish it the situation was more  akin to a human spotting a fly the fly  is being annoying so yes you have the  intent to kill it but that doesn't mean  that you punch it with all of your might  with that said all of meroram's  attributes will have a limit we just  aren't aware of what that limit is  because there was nothing in hunter  capable of pushing him to that point  which takes us to gone his adult form  much like marowan is an existence that  is extraordinarily difficult to quantify  the basic gist of the form is that gon  made an envow to access all of the power  he would ever have so what we're looking  at is a snapshot of what would have been  the future eventually gone would have  become a frankly unstoppable or a beast  and not only that but gone also grew to  physically surpass nephipito by an order  of magnitude which wouldn't have been so  difficult in terms of strength because  that comes quite handily with natural  enhancement but a very underrated aspect  about  gone is his speed and agility  particularly as pito is the most agile  of the three royal guards so seeing them  completely out class speaks volumes as  to what gon is capable of  and i really don't think it's out of the  question to put gone on relatively  the same playing field as base meruem in  that regard although there's no great  way to compare because the only other  two characters who outclassed pito's  speed were meruem himself and netero the  latter of whom having a particular level  of speed that not even meruem could  quite catch up to in the end not in his  base form anyway now before turning to  strength i think it's a bit more  important to consider aura because as a  natural enhancer that is more or less  going to directly convert into strength  for gone and the interesting thing about  the out of gone form is that it's not  clear if it has aural limitations mostly  due to killer's assessment of the  situation that the more oregon used in  this form the higher the price he would  ultimately need to pay perhaps meaning  that in theory gone could just keep  pushing into infinity kind of similarly  to alaka or i guess nanika's ability  they can make anything happen so long as  an equal price is paid although even  with that in mind i do strongly believe  that there would have been a strict  limitation somewhere with gone given  that he was only able to offer himself  up his payment still the aura reserves  that allocon possesses a pretty out of  control and will put him on a level of  strength comparable to that of meruem  via natural enhancement which by the way  is the one and only mild advantage that  gone actually has over marowan because  meruem is a natural specialist  so enhancement is by far his weakest  affinity meaning that there is a lot of  potential for gond close whatever that  power gap is with his natural boost  because it would basically cost meroem  several times as much aura as gone to  achieve the same effect and now  something else that will often get  brought up in regards to gone would be  the fact that pito did manage to sever  one of his arms or at least pito's  post-mortem post-moltemnen corpse thing  did this doesn't have any real impact on  his strength or durability because it  occurred at a moment where gon had  completely let his guard down  he thought that pito was dead and he was  an emotional wreck so no aura was being  expended to keep an eye on his  surroundings or defend himself and in  that situation  he suffered the same consequence as  anyone would have including meruem and i  suppose that brings us to where this  fight is ostensibly lost or won  and rather unsurprisingly for hunter  hunter it is entirely in the mental  arena because i do think that an  argument can be made that it is possible  for gon to have the strength speed and  aura reserves to take mariemon however  what he does not have  is the intellect to use those abilities  to actually overcome marijuana and this  isn't to say that gone is an air-headed  punch machine i actually don't think  gone gets anywhere near enough credit  for his intelligence he can be quite a  little genius in combat as shown time  and time again with particular examples  coming to mind being both against  genthru and knuckle however gone is a  very instinctual combatant  he acts based on more primal senses and  information which to be fair worked  phenomenally against nephipito gone  senses were unbelievably sharp in their  brief conflict and it really gave him  this truly invincible vibe however in  this case that would be pit directly  against meroram's strategic prowess  which is unmatched by all of humanity  well with one exception and only when it  comes to gungi specifically  marowam does have a greater advantage  though because his ridiculous  intelligence isn't all he has to rely on  being a chimera aunt he is also well and  truly in touch with the same sort of  primal instinct that gone heavily relies  on so gone doesn't have any particular  advantage there either oh and also we  should very much examine the motivation  of both characters because usually in  hypothetical combative discussions  that's less than relevant but the thing  to remember here is that the adult gone  form does not occur naturally this is  gone's response to the greatest despair  that he has ever felt in life as well as  his acceptance to relinquish his life  and i think that is best encapsulated  with the following line enough  let it end i don't care what happens to  me now i need all the power i'll ever  have which paints gone quite accurately  as a reckless revenge driven individual  which is a terrible match-up against  someone like meruem whose overbearing  sense of duty for his race will always  be able to overcome a self-destructive  mentality because really when it comes  down to it gone is fighting to die  whilst meruem is fighting to live and in  that situation both combatants would  achieve their goal making meroem the  easy winner and i do bring this up  because there is also a very common  misconception that gone transformed  because pito backed him into a corner  and threatened to kill him the general  logic being that this transformation was  more of a survival mechanism kicking in  and i really can't count the amount of  times that people have tried to tell me  this  but it's wrong during this conflict with  pito gone had one concern and that was  reviving kite once that became an  impossibility  gone made the decision to throw away his  life in order to take revenge  like he quite literally states that he  doesn't care what happens to himself the  thought of survival is so  far removed from what arogon is that he  would have been swiftly dissected by the  superior intellect and instinct of  meruem so the only path out of gon would  have to victory in this sort of  situation would be to have the strength  speed and aura so superior to meroems  that strategy becomes meaningless which  he certainly does not  so no matter what way we look at it this  encounter would greatly favor meruem  even if we were to accept the  hypothetical that gone's physical  abilities equally match those of the  king  because even in that situation the  mental mountain is simply too high for  gon to climb and that's probably one of  many reasons why togashi elected not to  have such a match-up in the series but  what do you guys think please do leave  your thoughts in the comments below or  even join my discord server and if  you're keen for some more hunt on  content then please to go and check out  some of my other videos or even  subscribe to the channel for regular  hunt hunter glory delivered straight  into your youtube feed but for now this  has been the new world review  and i'll see you next time

